From 920785731c15dc5cbd1c29997dfcf31e37680db7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wim Taymans <wtaymans@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:03:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] spa: v4l2: bound the chunk size by the v4l2 buffer length

The chunk size is clamped to the SPA buffer size but not to the length of
the V4L2 buffer.  When the SPA buffer is larger than the driver buffer,
the subsequent memcpy() reads past the end of the mmap()ed region.

Clamp to b->v4l2_buffer.length when it is known; the DMABUF path leaves
it zero.

See #5587

diff --git a/spa/plugins/v4l2/v4l2-utils.c b/spa/plugins/v4l2/v4l2-utils.c
index 2a5da7b5e..8d3ceda9e 100644
--- a/spa/plugins/v4l2/v4l2-utils.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/v4l2/v4l2-utils.c
@@ -1514,6 +1514,8 @@ static int mmap_read(struct impl *this)
 	d = b->outbuf->datas;
 	d[0].chunk->offset = 0;
 	d[0].chunk->size = SPA_MIN(buf.bytesused, d[0].maxsize);
+	if (b->v4l2_buffer.length > 0)
+		d[0].chunk->size = SPA_MIN(d[0].chunk->size, b->v4l2_buffer.length);
 	d[0].chunk->stride = port->fmt.fmt.pix.bytesperline;
 	d[0].chunk->flags = 0;
 	if (buf.flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR)

